From: loafecho <loafecho@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: intel-ipu4p: hold CPU latency at 100 us while ISYS is powered

Origin: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/discussions/1353
---
--- da/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-isys.c	2026-10-25 20:57:12.996038101 +0100
+++ db/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-isys.c	2026-10-25 20:57:13.017570102 +0100
@@ -32,7 +32,11 @@
 #include "ipu-platform.h"
 #include "ipu-platform-buttress-regs.h"
 
-#define ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE	300
+/*
+ * IPU4P: 300 us still allows Ice Lake C2 (exit 253 us) during streaming and
+ * stalls CSI. Hold at 100 us while ISYS is runtime-resumed (#1353 / loafecho).
+ */
+#define ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE	100
 
 /*
  * Convert firmware/ACPI CSI-2 port number to isys->csi2[] array index.
